  "title": "Eliminative Materialism",
  "role": "model",
  "summary": "Eliminative materialism, as Paul and Patricia Churchland set it out from 1981: folk psychology, the everyday framework of beliefs and desires, is an empirical theory, probably a radically false one, and its posits will be replaced, not reduced, by the concepts of a matured neuroscience. The mind is nothing more than what the brain does, and even the folk concept of consciousness may come apart.",
